            <ArticleTitle>Determination of a calibration factor for the nondestructive assay of Guidant 32P brachytherapy sources.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>835-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A calibration factor ('dial setting') for the nondestructive assay of Guidant TiNi-encapsulated 32P intravascular brachytherapy wire sources has been determined for measurements with the Capintec CRC-12 (sic. 'dose calibrator') ionization chamber. The calibration factor was derived from ionization current measurements with the CRC-12 followed by very quantitative, destructive assays of the 32P content in two sources.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
